| `template.manifest_differences.<path>` | object | keel's reasoned manifest differences; required by the parity test | `{"reason": "<non-blank>", "matches_when": [<condition>, ...]}`; `matches_when` is optional | `tests/integration/test_doc_drift.py::test_every_manifest_leaf_ships_in_both_manifest_twins`, from the loader-read manifest; no KEYS row | The test treats each key as an exact JSON Pointer into the manifest. The test decodes `~1` as `/` in a pointer. The test decodes `~0` as `~` in a pointer. The test renders `config/project.json.jinja` under each answer set that `answer_sets` in `tests/integration/test_reference_drift.py` derives from `copier.yml`. Those sets sample multiselect answers and hold free-text answers at their defaults, so they are not every valid Copier answer set. The test builds the expected manifest by replacing every occurrence of keel's `name` value inside string values with the answer `project_slug`, recursively through maps and lists. The test leaves map keys unchanged. The test compares maps key by key. The test compares lists as whole values. The test treats a different JSON type as a difference. The test treats two other values as equal only when their parsed Python types match and they compare equal, so the numbers `1` and `1.0` differ. The test reports a missing key once at that key's path. The test counts an exempted descendant of a missing key as differing when that descendant exists on either side. The test requires an exempted path to be equal on every answer set where all its `matches_when` conditions hold. The test allows an exempted path to differ on answer sets where any `matches_when` condition fails. The test reports an entry whose conditions hold on no answer set as a vacuous exemption. The test reports a non-vacuous entry whose path differs on no answer set where a condition fails as a stale exemption. The test requires an entry without `matches_when` to differ on every answer set. The test asks for `matches_when` when an unconditional entry is equal on some answer set. The test reports an unexempted difference by its path. The test reports the number of answer sets with that unexempted difference. The test reports a difference where `matches_when` holds with its answer-set count. The test includes one example answer set for a difference where `matches_when` holds. Generated manifests carry no `template` block. | classifying twin files: `template.twins` declares their purpose | keel maintainers only |
